#uuid "8f426df0-1f38-5a2e-b701-5e427a0357ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-139750" :question/problem "A biologist has recorded data on a pine tree's age (in years) and height (in feet). This data is shown below.\n\n| Age $(x)$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Height $(y)$ | $1.2$ | $2.5$ | $3.6$ | $4.5$ |\n\nFind the line of the form $y = β_{0} + β_{1}x$ that best fits the data above. According to the model, what will be the tree's height after $8$ years, assuming the trend continues?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that*\n$(X^{T}X)^{-1} = \\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}15 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}, X^{T}y = \\begin{bmatrix}11.8 \\\\ 35\\end{bmatrix}$,\n*where $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector.*\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092577 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd0b4da9-1a0f-5a46-aff1-3ce5c0cebb3b" :knowledge-point/title "Creating an Integral Expression For the Arc Length of a Polar Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9841d5a0-2d6c-5f87-a27a-f94eefabc095" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{π/2}e^{θ}\\sqrt{2θ^{2} + 4θ + 1}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089604} {:answer/id #uuid "29dd10e3-97bd-56a6-b470-31427419f7fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{π/2}e^{θ}\\sqrt{4θ^{2} + 2θ + 1}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089605} {:answer/id #uuid "33a3e6d0-52bd-58d1-a159-6de1f2c26ef9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{π/2}e^{θ}\\sqrt{θ^{2} + θ + 1}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089606} {:answer/id #uuid "5fbdd8df-eace-5463-a068-bbed35d03037" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{π/2}e^{θ}\\sqrt{2θ^{2} + 2θ + 1}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089607} {:answe