" :question/math-academy-id "q-158314" :question/problem "![](images/b9/b95c538613ee8672e0f1cac970b7af230ec40bf3075e609b1e03f7cad4382fb1.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is\n$intA = {(x, y) ∈ R^{2}: 0 < x < 1, A A A A A}$.\nWhat is the missing expression?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152438 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db20f4a5-27a4-5fbc-aae2-2febf8f99cb1" :knowledge-point/title "The Parametric Equations of an Ellipse Centered at the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6d1de36-c45f-576e-a7f1-ddd4556e6e6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 4\\cos θ, y = 49\\sin θ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149130} {:answer/id #uuid "a6e6c06b-fbd2-58df-8e45-287b8f1bd672" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 2\\sin θ, y = 7\\cos θ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149131} {:answer/id #uuid "a9f202dd-0ca4-50e2-93ae-12d42b873745" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 7\\cos θ, y = 2\\sin θ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149132} {:answer/id #uuid "bebafa99-24a7-5707-8536-24d126c9d58f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 7\\sin θ, y = 2\\cos θ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149133} {:answer/id #uuid "7d9a2b8e-346c-559b-aa35-5c942ebd9ad7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 2\\cos θ, y = 7\\sin θ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149134}] :answer-field/id #uuid "c9d808a2-555f-5182-9d76-592cf8cf6ea8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149129}] :question/id #uuid "46c88046-0f62-50bb-8a31-ae13a6c535ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-15856" :question/problem "![](images/0c/0c46972a3968d7110cb08d4b16bfff9267e49b102cf005cdbb21a3630d15c49d.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse centered at the origin with horizontal radius $7$ and vertical radius $2$, as shown above. Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $θ ∈ [0, 2π)$, traverse the ellipse once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(7, 0)$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172381 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5256297-c928-54e3-bf4d-35f5734f5632" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing Surface Integrals Over Parametric Surfaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9be70133-e143-555a-b316-c857cb78e325" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u^{2}v^{2}\\sqrt{u^{2} + v^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169120} {:answer/id #uuid "a6c62bb4-f2b7-5a28-bab7-5df3a9504149" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "uv\\sqrt{u^{2} + v^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169121} {:answer/id #uuid "cdf2f94a-1a8b-5d99-8a70-f07f6c82f8fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u^{2}v^{2}\\sqrt{uv}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169122} {:answer/id #uuid "0966e2fa-eeb2-5012-9af2-d57f5e7b0e1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u^{2}v^{2}\\sqrt{u + v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169123} {:answer/id #uuid "2e1bec9b-3572-5c9b-a9e1-b8bf0036f7d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "uv\\sqrt{uv}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169124}] :answer-field/id #uuid "8b5413c5-cd70-5f06-8ea5-ec7c6d11e516" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169119}] :question/id #uuid "25e44fde-444d-5880-ba2e-43dd4bc039db" :question/math-academy-id "q-160711" :question/problem "$∬_(S)f(x, y, z)dS = ∬_(D)AAAAAAAdA$\nConsider the surface integral of the function\n$f(x, y, z) = xyz$\nover the parametric surface\n$r(u, v) = ⟨u, v, uv⟩$\nfor $(u, v) ∈ D⊆R^{2}$. What is the missing expression?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167132 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21caaf9c-6b9b-5711-a434-21f0416e6c7e" :knowledge-point/title "Rewriting a Flux Integral as a Surface Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0f632e1-bc4a-5e20-9d42-993ea0ac140f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{2} + 2yz" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163841} {:answer/id #uuid "d9597573-13cf-5b29-80fc-a0cec25c3d02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{2} + yz" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163842} {:answer/id #uuid "dcf7721d-433b-562f-8b02-6dc0eaf18ebf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy - yz + 2xz" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163843} {:answer/id #uuid "f8a59231-39be-5bd9-b000-7fd5bea7b50b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy + yz + xz" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163844} {:answer/id #uuid "0cfc1e63-d79d-5c0a-a85e-bb0f5321e73a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{2} + 3yz" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163845}] :answer-field/id #uuid "800fbb75-73ff-5c83-b570-3144244101d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163840}] :question/id #uuid "7492e5fe-6cc9-5d4b-8d1f-20d212147cee" :question/math-academy-id "q-160838" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with normal vector $n^(~)$, where\n\n$F(x, y, z) = ⟨z, y, x⟩, n^(~)(x, y, z) = ⟨2y,-z, 2x⟩, n = (n^(~))/(‖n^(~)‖)$.\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$∬_(S)F \\cdot dS = ∬_(S)\\frac{AAAAAAA}{\\sqrt{4x^{2} + 4y^{2} + z^{2}}}dS$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129532 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b4a31c6-01be-5b15-88f5-9150f350e944" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Critical Points of a Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9ef2524-c316-5f5c-bb17-9410d6df7855" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $u = 2v$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126662} {:answer/id #uuid "af21f9b2-947b-5b4b-9b83-b2324aabe6c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the parabolic cylinder $u =-w^{2}$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126663} {:answer/id #uuid "b8ef1406-0abe-5cfe-bc04-7ae04a77ecf5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $u = w$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126664} {:answer/id #uuid "e90dd075-4fb2-51bb-9367-44b42c15619d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $vw -$plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126665} {:answer/id #uuid "0cffeeef-f100-51b5-ac9e-aa76adbf7807" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the parabolic cylinder $u = 2w^{2}$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126666}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4d271abc-b1d9-5284-9062-68834149c800" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126661}] :question/id #uuid "685e989d-8721-5a8c-a4d8-0e44efe4bc9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-161819" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T$, where $T$ is defined as\n\n$T: \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u^{2} - w^{2} \\\\ we^{u} \\\\ u - v\\end{bmatrix}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106074 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fea43b6-fd7b-5edc-b6b7-7f8b2cbab502" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Type of Image Formed by a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bb34d14-4e6b-5921-bbae-0804ad06b4f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A triangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102301} {:answer/id #uuid "b2b33753-c1ca-54f2-b9c6-98ba27f6fa8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A rectangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102302} {:answer/id #uuid "cb1ac350-98a0-5f6c-8490-7f08a97c5de0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "A line segment" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102303} {:answer/id #uuid "1338e2d6-47